    <string name="faq_q_connect">How do I connect to the VPN?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_connect">On the home screen, tap the big round button. A server is picked automatically, but you can change it in the server list.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_slow">Can\'t connect or the speed is slow</string>
    <string name="faq_a_slow">Switch to a server with a lower ping. If that doesn\'t help, reconnect or restart the app.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_server">How do I change the server?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_server">Tap the server card on the home screen and pick one from the list.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_pay">How do I pay for, renew or change a subscription?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_pay">Open the Subscription card on the home screen, pick the plan you need and tap Buy — Telegram opens for payment. You can also renew or switch your plan in the same place.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_activate">My subscription didn\'t activate after payment</string>
    <string name="faq_a_activate">Wait a couple of minutes and pull down to refresh. If the status doesn\'t change, message support.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_traffic">When does the traffic limit reset?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_traffic">Your traffic limit in GB resets once a month: the counter goes back to zero and the full amount becomes available again.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_devices">How do I add a second device?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_devices">Open Advanced → Devices, then scan the QR code or enter the code from the new device.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_privacy">Is my data safe?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_privacy">All traffic is encrypted and we don\'t keep logs of your network activity.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_platforms">Which platforms is the app available on?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_platforms">The app is available on Android, Android TV, Windows and Linux.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_stores">Why isn\'t the app on Google Play or the App Store?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_stores">The app is being published to Google Play and will be available there soon. An App Store version will come later. For now, updates are handled right in the app.</string>
