    <string name="diagnostics_info_button">How diagnostics works</string>
    <string name="diagnostics_info_title">Diagnostic mode</string>
    <string name="diagnostics_info_manual">Enabling diagnostic mode only reveals these controls. Recording starts separately when you tap “Start collection”.</string>
    <string name="diagnostics_info_persistence">Once started manually, collection continues after an app restart and while the VPN is running in the background until you stop it or disable diagnostic mode.</string>
    <string name="diagnostics_info_contents">The log records VPN startup and shutdown stages, core state, network changes, background tunnel checks, server refresh and availability, TCP latency, session traffic volume and actual uplink/downlink rate, and the result of a manually started speed test. Hidden background speed tests are never started.</string>
    <string name="diagnostics_info_daily">A separate log of up to 10 MB is created for each day. Up to 7 latest daily logs are kept in the app\'s private storage; older logs are removed automatically.</string>
    <string name="diagnostics_info_privacy">The journal contains technical app and VPN state events only. It does not record traffic contents, visited addresses, tokens, account IDs, server addresses, or VPN configuration.</string>
    <string name="diagnostics_info_share">ToBeVPN never sends logs automatically. In “Log history” you can share or permanently delete each daily log yourself.</string>
